on september 12 2017 tim cook came out  on stage and revealed apple's iphone 10  which came with the groundbreaking new  face id authentication system that we  all know and love today but  unfortunately it required apple to cut  out a notch out of the display to fit in  their full array of true depth sensors  including the dot projector that  projects a ton of little dots onto your  face which are then scanned by the  infrared camera to measure the depth of  your facial features and confirm that it  is in fact you who's unlocking the  iphone and now four years later face id  works great and all but people are  honestly getting sick of seeing this  huge notch on their iphone while the  competition like samsung's galaxy vol 3  is already using under display camera  technology that definitely isn't perfect  due to the horrible camera quality but  it's definitely way ahead of apple's  massive notch so with that said apple's  new smaller notch on the iphone 13 is  both a good thing and a bad thing  because while we're all happy that the  notch is getting smaller we all honestly  wish apple would have gotten rid of it  completely by now so in this video i'm  gonna share the truth about what apple  is doing with the smaller notch and why  including how this changes everything  for the future when apple eventually  switches to a new cutout design before  getting rid of it completely so let's  get started first off if you're  wondering why apple is taking so long to  get rid of the notch i need to teach you  a little lesson about how apple does  marketing the most important thing about  how apple designs their products is that  they stand out from the crowd when you  see this in somebody's ears you know  it's a pair of airpods 100 guaranteed no  doubt about it when you see a computer  like this you know it's an imac due to  the iconic chin that many people wish  apple would get rid of but they won't  when you see this pair of headphones  you know it's apple's airpods max due to  the all-aluminum finish the color scheme  and the unique headband design when you  see this watch on somebody's wrist you  know it's an apple watch and when you  see a smartphone with a notch that looks  like this you know it's an iphone 100  guaranteed even from a block away so yes  apple likes to make their products stand  out and to do that sometimes their  designs can be a little bit shocking  like the original airpods which  countless people made fun of but it's  the very reason why they went viral  people also went crazy over the  tripophobic triple lens design on the  back of the iphone 11 but it stands out  from the rest of the camera bump designs  on the market so if you're wondering why  apple is keeping the notch around on the  iphone 13 i have a couple of very good  reasons for it obviously the notch is  gonna help the iphone continue to stand  out from the crowd which apple loves to  do but on the other hand the smaller  notch is gonna appeal to a lot of the  iphone users who have been waiting for  that design change before upgrading  again since it's gonna make it look  quite a bit better and the other good  reason that people forget about is that  apple needs to continue selling iphones  for the next decade so if they  completely got rid of the notch in just  one year there's gonna be nothing left  for them to change or improve the next  year so from apple's perspective they  need to carefully improve the display  and the notch on the iphone over the  course of a few years so they have a  clear path of upgrade ability to be able  to extract more sales and profits but  with all that said and out of the way i  want to now get into the details about  this notch that are going to be  incredibly important for the future if  you look at the design of the smaller  notch you'll see that the absolutely  biggest change is the relocation of the  speaker grille up to the top of the  phone right underneath the frame if you  think about it if apple was to create a  completely notchless phone in the future  the speaker grille absolutely had to be  moved up to the top which they've  thankfully already done on the iphone  13. so this is a very important step to  get rid of the notch completely on top  of that way back in january it was  reported that apple would be redesigning  the face id sensor system by integrating  three of the main truedepth sensors into  just one camera module to enable the  smaller knot size and this has recently  been confirmed by john prosser who was  able to get his hands on images of a new  device that apple is handing out to  employees that features the brand new  face id system and that actually matches  up to the leaked notch photos that we've  seen in the past and the reason why  apple is handing this out to employees  is because apparently the new face id  system is going to work with masks which  is by far the biggest complaint that  people have with face id and it's also  the main reason why people are asking  for in-display touch id but the truth is  if apple is able to make face id work  with mass then there's really no reason  for touch id anymore at least in my  opinion but the point that i'm trying to  make is that apple is working on  consolidating the face id system into  less and less cutouts which is gonna  greatly help them in the future when  they try to completely go notchless and  if you really think about it the lidar  scanner on the back of the iphone is  basically a face id sensor system built  into just one cutout so i fully expect  apple to do this with the front of the  display with face id but now i want to  get into a major leak that i've recently  discovered that apparently nobody is  talking about according to the  lesser-known leaker shrimp apple pro his  sources are claiming that the iphone 14  is gonna have a double punch hole notch  design and if this sounds absolutely  crazy to you check out this leak from a  few months back from ming chi quo who is  a pretty reliable analyst he said that  some 2022 iphone 14 models are gonna  abandon the notch in favor of a punch  hole display  matching up to the other leak and if you  think about it apple is not going to be  able to put all those sensors into just  one cutout so they need a double cutout  design and if you're wondering what  that's going to look like philip  vabrosic on twitter created a render of  the double cutout showing what it could  potentially look like and i could  definitely agree that it looks better  than the notch and it also looks unique  compared to other phones out there but  then the big game changer leak was when  shrimp apple pro leaked an image of a  prototype iphone 14 display panel that  could actually be legit  but of course this isn't coming from a  reputable leaker so we can't really take  it too seriously and going further  apparently minxiko believes that at  least one iphone 15 model in 2023  is gonna have a completely notchless  design which would mean that the sensors  are going underneath the display but in  my opinion i don't know if i agree with  both the leaker and ming chi quo about  this whole new punch hole design coming  to the iphone 14 and a notchless design  coming to the iphone 15. to me it  doesn't make sense for apple to spend  three years with the same exact notch on  the iphone 10 through 12 only to  redesign the notch and make it smaller  on the 13 and then switch to a cutout  design for the 14 and then go completely  notchless for the 15. moving at such a  quick pace doesn't really sound like  something apple would do so in my  opinion it makes sense for the iphone  13's smaller notch to also come on the  iphone 14 because we already know that  the 14 is going to be focused on massive  camera improvements including a 48  megapixel camera that can shoot 8k video  and then the iphone 15 will probably  come with this new dual cutout design  and then the completely nauseous design  will come sometime after that but either  way all of this can only be made  possible by the huge changes that apple  is making to the iphone 13's notch by  moving the speaker up to the top of the  phone and consolidating a bunch of face  id sensors into one so with that i'm  excited to see what the future holds for  the iphone if you enjoyed this video go  ahead and tap the like button and click  the circle button to subscribe for more  videos like this one and definitely  check out one of those two right over  there thanks for watching and we'll see  you in the next video  [Music]
 

